1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:05,479
Chapter 2. The carpet bag.

2
00:00:05,480 --> 00:00:10,279
I stuffed a shirt or two into my old carpet bag, tucked it under my arm, and

3
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:12,598
started for Cape Horn in the Pacific.

4
00:00:12,599 --> 00:00:18,598
Quitting the good city of old Manhattan, I duly arrived in New Bedford. It was a

5
00:00:18,599 --> 00:00:22,678
Saturday night in December. Much was I disappointed upon learning that the

6
00:00:22,679 --> 00:00:27,317
little packet for Nantucket had already sailed, and that no way of reaching that

7
00:00:27,318 --> 00:00:32,279
place would offer till the following Monday, as most candidates for the pains

8
00:00:32,280 --> 00:00:36,759
and penalties of wailing stop at this same New Bedford then to embark on their

9
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:42,837
voyage, it may as well be related that I, for one, had no idea of so doing, for

10
00:00:42,838 --> 00:00:47,718
my mind was made up to sail in no other than a Nantucket craft, because there

11
00:00:47,719 --> 00:00:52,038
was a fine, boisterous something about everything connected with that famous

12
00:00:52,039 --> 00:00:55,558
old island which amazingly pleased me.

13
00:00:55,559 --> 00:01:00,357
Besides, though New Bedford has of late been gradually monopolizing the business

14
00:01:00,358 --> 00:01:05,399
of whailing, and though in this matter poor old Nantucket is now much behind

15
00:01:05,400 --> 00:01:10,837
her, yet Nantucket was her great original, the tire of this Carthage, the

16
00:01:10,838 --> 00:01:15,399
place where the first dead American whale was stranded. Where else but from

17
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:20,598
Nantucket did those Aboriginal whalemen, the red men, first sally out in canoes

18
00:01:20,599 --> 00:01:25,317
to give chase to the Leviathan? And where but from Nantucket too, did that

19
00:01:25,318 --> 00:01:29,799
first adventurous little sloop put forth, partly laden with imported

20
00:01:29,800 --> 00:01:34,598
cobblestones, so goes the story, to throw at the whales, in order to

21
00:01:34,599 --> 00:01:39,799
discover when they were nigh enough to risk a harpoon from the bowsprit.

22
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:44,118
Now having a night, a day, and still another night following before me in New

23
00:01:44,119 --> 00:01:49,238
Bedford, air I could embark for my destined port, it became a matter of

24
00:01:49,239 --> 00:01:54,518
concernment where I was to eat and sleep. Meanwhile, it was a very dubiousl

25
00:01:54,519 --> 00:02:00,118
looking, nay, a very dark and dismal night, bitingly cold and cheerless. I

26
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:05,317
knew no one in the place. With anxious grapes, I had sounded my pocket and only

27
00:02:05,318 --> 00:02:10,759
brought up a few pieces of silver. So wherever you go, Ishmael, said I to

28
00:02:10,760 --> 00:02:15,558
myself, as I stood in the middle of a dreary street, shouldering my bag, and

29
00:02:15,559 --> 00:02:20,357
comparing the gloom toward the north with the darkness towards the south.

30
00:02:20,358 --> 00:02:25,799
Wherever in your wisdom you may conclude to lodge for the night, my dear Ishmael,

31
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:31,238
be sure to inquire the price, and don't be too particular.

32
00:02:31,239 --> 00:02:36,279
With halting steps I paced the streets and passed the sign of the cross

33
00:02:36,280 --> 00:02:42,038
tarpoons, but it looked too expensive and jolly there. Further on, from the

34
00:02:42,039 --> 00:02:47,238
bright red windows of the swordfish inn, there came such fervent rays that it

35
00:02:47,239 --> 00:02:51,479
seemed to have melted the packed snow and ice before the house, for everywhere

36
00:02:51,480 --> 00:02:57,879
else the congealed frost lay 10 in thick in a hard asphaltic pavement, rather

37
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:02,518
weary for me when I struck my foot against the flinty projections, because

38
00:03:02,519 --> 00:03:06,919
from hard, remorseless service the souls of my boots were in a most miserable

39
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:12,919
plight. Too expensive and jolly again, thought I, pausing one moment to watch

40
00:03:12,920 --> 00:03:17,238
the broad glare in the street and hear the sounds of the tinkling glasses

41
00:03:17,239 --> 00:03:22,678
within. But go on, Ishmael, said I, at last, don't you hear? Get away from

42
00:03:22,679 --> 00:03:29,078
before the door. Your patched boots are stopping the way. So on I went. I now by

43
00:03:29,079 --> 00:03:33,479
instinct followed the streets that took me waterward, for there doubtless were

44
00:03:33,480 --> 00:03:37,317
