45
00:03:37,318 --> 00:03:42,439
such dreary streets, blocks of blackness, not houses, on either hand,

46
00:03:42,440 --> 00:03:47,317
and here and there a candle like a candle moving about in a tomb. At this

47
00:03:47,318 --> 00:03:51,399
hour of the night, of the last day of the week, that quarter of the town

48
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:56,919
proved all but deserted, but presently I came to a smoky light proceeding from a

49
00:03:56,920 --> 00:04:02,598
low, wide building, the door of which stood invitingly open. It had a careless

50
00:04:02,599 --> 00:04:07,078
look, as if it were meant for the uses of the public. So entering, the first

51
00:04:07,079 --> 00:04:13,158
thing I did was to stumble over an ash box in the porch. Ha, thought I. Ha, as

52
00:04:13,159 --> 00:04:15,718
the flying particles almost choked me.

53
00:04:15,719 --> 00:04:20,999
Are these ashes from that destroyed city, Gamora? But the cross tarpoons and

54
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:27,078
the swordfish, this then must needs be the sign of the trap. However, I picked

55
00:04:27,079 --> 00:04:34,198
myself up and hearing a loud voice within, pushed on and opened a second interior door.

56
00:04:34,199 --> 00:04:38,518
It seemed a great black parliament sitting in Tophett. A hundred black

57
00:04:38,519 --> 00:04:43,959
faces turned round in their rows to peer, and beyond a black angel of doom

58
00:04:43,960 --> 00:04:48,678
was beating a book in the pulpit. It was a negro church, and the preacher's text

59
00:04:48,679 --> 00:04:53,399
was about the blackness of darkness and the weeping and wailing and teeth

60
00:04:53,400 --> 00:04:58,118
nashing there. Ha!" Ishmael muttered eye, backing out, "Wretched

61
00:04:58,119 --> 00:05:01,638
entertainment at the sign of the trap."

62
00:05:01,639 --> 00:05:06,999
Moving on, I at last came to a dim sort of light, not far from the docks, and

63
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:12,198
heard a forlorn creaking in the air, and looking up, saw a swinging sign over the

64
00:05:12,199 --> 00:05:16,357
door with a white painting on it, faintly representing a tall, straight

65
00:05:16,358 --> 00:05:23,799
jet of misty spray, and these words underneath, "The Spouter Inn. Peter Coffin."

66
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:30,038
coffin spout. rather ominous in that particular connection, thought I, but it

67
00:05:30,039 --> 00:05:34,678
is a common name in Nantucket, they say, and I suppose this Peter here is an

68
00:05:34,679 --> 00:05:38,919
immigrant from there, as the light looked so dim, and the place for the

69
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:42,919
time looked quiet enough, and the dilapidated little wooden house itself

70
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:46,759
looked as if it might have been carted here from the ruins of some burnt

71
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:52,518
district, and as the swinging sign had a poverty-stricken sort of creek to it, I

72
00:05:52,519 --> 00:05:58,518
thought that here was the very spot for cheap lodgings, and the best of pea coffee.

73
00:05:58,519 --> 00:06:03,718
It was a queer sort of place, a gable-ended old house, one side Paulied

74
00:06:03,719 --> 00:06:09,317
as it were, and leaning over sadly. It stood on a sharp, bleak corner, where

75
00:06:09,318 --> 00:06:14,837
that tempestuous windon kept up a worse howling than ever it did about poor

76
00:06:14,838 --> 00:06:20,919
Paul's tossed craft. Uralon nevertheless is a mighty pleasant zephr to anyone

77
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:26,038
indoors, with his feet on the hob, quietly toasting for bed.

78
00:06:26,039 --> 00:06:31,718
In judging of that tempestuous wind called Uraladon, says an old writer, of

79
00:06:31,719 --> 00:06:37,078
whose works I possess the only copy extent, it maketh a marvelous difference

80
00:06:37,079 --> 00:06:41,158
whether thou lookst out at it from a glass window where the frost is all on

81
00:06:41,159 --> 00:06:46,198
the outside, or whether thou observest it from that sashless window, where the

82
00:06:46,199 --> 00:06:52,118
frost is on both sides, and of which the white death is the only glaze.

83
00:06:52,119 --> 00:06:57,158
True enough, thought I, as this passage occurred to my mind. Old black letter

84
00:06:57,159 --> 00:07:02,518
thou reasonest well. Yes, these eyes are windows, and this body of mine is the

85
00:07:02,519 --> 00:07:07,399
house. What a pity they didn't stop up the chinks in the crannies, though, and

86
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,959
